[
    [
        {
            "type": "header",
            "bbox": [
                0.37,
                0.042,
                0.628,
                0.082
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "WT/DS622/R\nBCI deleted, as indicated [[***]]\n- 66 -"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.114,
                0.1,
                0.883,
                0.156
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "substantiate its submission by explaining how the European Commission failed to act consistently with Articles 3.1 and 3.4 by rejecting KLK's submission for the reasons that it did. In particular, Indonesia does not substantiate why the European Commission's overall analysis on injury was undermined by the views set by one of the producers in this letter.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.167,
                0.883,
                0.209
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.277. For the foregoing reasons, we find that Indonesia has not established that the European Commission failed to give appropriate weight, in its overall assessment of the state of the domestic industry, to factors displaying a positive trend.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.22,
                0.882,
                0.248
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.6 Indonesia's consequential claims under Article 1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement and Article VI of the GATT 1994",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.26,
                0.883,
                0.302
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.278. Indonesia contends that as a consequence of the substantive violations under the Anti-Dumping Agreement and the GATT 1994, the European Union acted inconsistently with Article 1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement and Article VI of the GATT 1994. \\( ^{400} \\)",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.313,
                0.883,
                0.356
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.279. We note that Indonesia's claim under Article 1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement is a purely consequential one. As a consequence of the substantive violations that we found above, we find that the European Commission also acted inconsistently with Article 1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.114,
                0.366,
                0.884,
                0.487
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "7.280. With respect to Indonesia's consequential claim under Article VI of the GATT 1994, in presenting this consequential claim Indonesia does not identify the specific paragraphs of Article VI, or the specific obligations that it seeks to challenge. Like the panel in US – OCTG (Korea), we do not consider that we can make findings under Article VI in general, or parse the complainant's claim to identify which obligations in Article VI are violated as a consequence of the substantive violations. \\( ^{401} \\)  Therefore, we reject this consequential claim under Article VI. Nonetheless, we note that we found, for the reasons set out above, a violation under Article VI:2 of the GATT 1994 because the anti-dumping duty imposed on Musim Mas was based on a margin of dumping calculated inconsistently with Article 2.4.1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.116,
                0.498,
                0.483,
                0.513
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "8 CONCLUSIONS AND RECOMMENDATION"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.525,
                0.882,
                0.552
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "8.1. For the reasons set out in this Report, we conclude that the European Union acted inconsistently with:",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.163,
                0.566,
                0.883,
                0.607
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "a. Article 2.4.1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement because of the European Commission's failure to use the rate of exchange on the date of sale as required by this Article \\( ^{402} \\) ;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.163,
                0.618,
                0.883,
                0.673
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "b. Article 9.3 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement and Article VI:2 of the GATT 1994 by imposing an anti-dumping duty exceeding the margin of dumping that should have been established under Article 2 due to the inconsistency with Article 2.4.1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement as set out in paragraph 8.1(a) above \\( ^{403} \\) ; and",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.163,
                0.685,
                0.863,
                0.7
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "c. Article 1 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement as a consequence of these inconsistencies. \\( ^{404} \\)",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.712,
                0.882,
                0.74
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "8.2. For the reasons set out in this Report, we conclude that Indonesia has failed to establish that the European Union acted inconsistently with:",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.163,
                0.752,
                0.882,
                0.781
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "a. Article 5.6 of the Anti-Dumping Agreement by continuing the anti-dumping investigation on imports of fatty acid despite the withdrawal of the written application \\( ^{405} \\) ;",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footnote",
            "bbox": [
                0.161,
                0.809,
                0.581,
                0.823
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "\\( ^{400} \\)  Indonesia's first written submission, paras. 310 and 370."
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footnote",
            "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.821,
                0.868,
                0.868
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "\\( ^{401} \\)  Panel Report, US – OCTG (Korea), para. 7.337. We are aware that some other panels have found consequential violations under Article VI as a whole, but do not consider such an approach to be warranted in this dispute. (See e.g. Panel Reports, China – HP-SSST (Japan) / China – HP-SSST (EU), para. 7.336; and Canada – Welded Pipe, para. 7.223)"
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footnote",
            "bbox": [
                0.163,
                0.868,
                0.354,
                0.882
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "\\( ^{402} \\)  See para. 7.185 above."
        },
